---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/blog-article.css';

const pageTitle = 'What Is RSVP Reading? Rapid Serial Visual Presentation Explained | BriskRead';
const pageDescription =
  'RSVP reading explained: how flashing words at a fixed point works, ORP highlights, when RSVP helps, and when full-page Focus is better.';
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <article class="blog-article mt-8">
    <div class="container max-w-3xl">
      <div class="glass glass-article">
        <p class="section-label">Concepts</p>
        <h1>What is RSVP reading?</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          RSVP means <strong>Rapid Serial Visual Presentation</strong>: words appear one after another at a fixed place on the screen so your eyes stop hunting along a line. It is the core of many online flash readers, including Flash mode in <a href="/rsvp-reader">BriskRead’s RSVP reader</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How RSVP works</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Text is split into words (or short phrases)</li>
          <li>Each unit is shown for a duration based on your WPM</li>
          <li>A focal letter (often the Optimal Recognition Point) is emphasized</li>
          <li>Punctuation can add a brief pause so meaning can land</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Why people use it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Less horizontal eye movement (saccades)</li>
          <li>Harder to re-read the same line by habit</li>
          <li>Clearer sense of pace than free scrolling</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Limits of RSVP</h2>
        <p>
          RSVP is not magic. On unfamiliar, formula-heavy, or legal text, forced flash speed can destroy comprehension. That is why serious tools also offer <a href="/how-it-works">Focus, Flow, Bionic, and Page modes</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>RSVP + audio</h2>
        <p>
          Pairing RSVP with speech (Audio Sync) is dual-channel presentation: vision and hearing track the same token stream. See <a href="/blog/audio-sync-speed-reading">why that matters</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            Demo RSVP free on the <a href="/">BriskRead homepage</a> — start around 350 WPM and lower the slider until words stay meaningful.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="article-footer">
          <p>Related: <a href="/blog/best-online-speed-readers">Best online speed readers</a> · <a href="/bionic-reading">Bionic reading</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
